  "verbalization": "Trichostatin A appears to interact with CD276 antigen through a series of molecular pathways, with SK-MEL-2 cells serving as a key intermediate. The evidence suggests that Trichostatin A targets SK-MEL-2, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Lagunamide B and Ziziphin. Both of these compounds ultimately direct their activity toward CD276 antigen. This indicates that Trichostatin A may exert its effects on CD276 through a shared mechanism involving SK-MEL-2, potentially by modulating the expression or activity of CD276 in this cell line. The presence of multiple pathways converging on CD276 suggests a complex regulatory network, possibly involving post-translational modifications or signaling cascades that are not fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of SK-MEL-2 as a central node in the interaction between Trichostatin A and CD276.",
